Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:04.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The ocean absorbs a large share of humanity's carbon emissions,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.95,0:00:10.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}yet our official picture of how much it takes up always lags reality by about a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.95,0:00:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This work introduces Carbon Monitor Ocean, or CMO-NRT, a near-real-time, monthly,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.66,0:00:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}gridded dataset of global surface ocean fugacity of CO2 and air-sea CO2 flux.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.10,0:00:28.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}By using convolutional neural networks and semi-supervised learning to update the estimates
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.52,0:00:32.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}from ten ocean biogeochemical models and eight data products,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.82,0:00:37.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the authors extend the global carbon budget to the present month,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.41,0:00:43.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}giving scientists and policymakers a far more timely view of the ocean carbon sink.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.57,0:00:47.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The ocean is one of the largest buffers against climate change,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.86,0:00:51.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}soaking up a big fraction of the carbon dioxide we emit.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.66,0:00:55.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But our best official accounting of how much it absorbs,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.47,0:01:00.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the annual Global Carbon Budget, always trails reality by about a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.30,0:01:03.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}That means when the ocean's uptake shifts,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.16,0:01:06.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}we simply cannot see it until long after the fact.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.56,0:01:11.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This lag is baked in: the biogeochemical models are computationally heavy,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.60,0:01:17.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the surface-ocean observations they rely on are themselves delayed by roughly a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.95,0:01:22.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}As countries move through the global stocktake under the Paris Agreement,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.52,0:01:26.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}they need to know where the carbon is going right now, not a year ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.89,0:01:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The existing databases of ocean carbon fluxes are detailed and trustworthy,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.58,0:01:34.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but they are always looking backward in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.40,0:01:38.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}What is missing is a way to bring that same rigor up to the present month,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.03,0:01:44.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so that policymakers and scientists can respond to changes in the ocean sink as they happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.08,0:01:51.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The core contribution is Carbon Monitor Ocean, or CMO-NRT: a near-real-time, monthly,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.09,0:01:56.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}gridded dataset of global surface ocean carbon dioxide fugacity and air-sea flux,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.81,0:02:01.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}together with the machine-learning framework that generates it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.26,0:02:04.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Rather than replace the trusted community models,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.72,0:02:10.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it updates all ten ocean biogeochemical models and eight data products from the Global
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.80,0:02:14.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Carbon Budget 2022 into a near-real-time framework.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.40,0:02:20.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The dataset and the code are released openly, on Figshare and on the project website.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.71,0:02:26.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The method treats each biogeochemical model or data product as a target that a neural
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.37,0:02:30.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}network learns to reproduce from observable predictors: year,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.44,0:02:32.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}month, latitude, longitude,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.24,0:02:36.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and nine environmental variables like sea-surface temperature, salinity,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.04,0:02:38.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}chlorophyll and wind.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.44,0:02:46.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Global grids are cut into small eighteen-by-eighteen patches and fed through stacked convolutional and linear layers.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.23,0:02:52.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The clever part is semi-supervised learning: alongside a standard supervised error on labeled points,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.96,0:02:58.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the model adds an unsupervised consistency loss that forces its predictions to agree when
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.89,0:03:03.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}ten percent versus thirty percent of the input features are masked.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.36,0:03:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Combining the two losses makes the model markedly more stable.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.79,0:03:10.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The resulting dataset delivers monthly,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.64,0:03:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}gridded maps of global surface-ocean carbon dioxide fugacity and air-sea flux,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.33,0:03:19.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}spanning January 2022 through July 2023,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.25,0:03:27.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}built by updating the ten ocean biogeochemical models and eight data products of the Global Carbon Budget 2022.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.35,0:03:33.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Its inputs draw on satellite and reanalysis products for chlorophyll, temperature,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.33,0:03:38.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}sea ice, mixed-layer depth, salinity, sea-surface height, pressure and wind,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.88,0:03:45.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the whole dataset is published openly on Figshare and refreshed on the project website.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.82,0:03:47.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To test the approach,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.19,0:03:51.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the authors held out the most recent two years of every model and product,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.03,0:03:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}trained only on earlier data, and then predicted the withheld period.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.54,0:04:02.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The predictions track the originals remarkably well: for most of the ten models and eight products,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.00,0:04:06.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the correlation exceeds an R-squared of point nine,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.34,0:04:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and even the global monthly aggregates mostly stay above point eight five.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.17,0:04:14.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On global averages the predictions run just slightly high,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.96,0:04:18.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with most differences smaller than three microatmospheres.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.05,0:04:24.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Looking model by model reveals a clear pattern: the biogeochemical models are reproduced
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.78,0:04:26.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}most faithfully and consistently,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.93,0:04:30.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with several exceeding an R-squared of point nine five,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.51,0:04:36.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while a few data products are noisier and occasionally scatter away from the fit line.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.12,0:04:41.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Spatial maps of the differences confirm that agreement is broadly uniform across the globe,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.04,0:04:47.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with the largest residual gaps concentrated in the Arctic Ocean and the equatorial Pacific.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.27,0:04:50.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A few numbers capture the impact.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.57,0:04:55.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The method collapses the roughly one-year reporting delay down to monthly,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.73,0:05:00.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}near-real-time coverage, here spanning January 2022 through July 2023.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.61,0:05:07.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Validation correlations exceed an R-squared of point nine for most of the eighteen source estimates,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.58,0:05:10.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}global aggregates stay above point eight five,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.79,0:05:15.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and global monthly differences are mostly under three microatmospheres.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.74,0:05:22.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Even the auxiliary near-real-time atmospheric carbon dioxide model achieves a root-mean-square
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.30,0:05:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}error of just one point seven four,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.74,0:05:26.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}about a half-percent error.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.92,0:05:32.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The takeaway is simple: by pairing convolutional networks with semi-supervised learning
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.53,0:05:35.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}to update trusted models and data products,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.31,0:05:42.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Carbon Monitor Ocean turns a once year-delayed picture of the global ocean carbon sink into a near-real-time,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.34,0:05:43.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}monthly, gridded monitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.95,0:05:49.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}That gives scientists and policymakers a far timelier and spatially detailed constraint
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.56,0:05:52.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}on how much carbon the ocean is taking up,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.27,0:05:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}right when they need it for the carbon budget and climate decisions.
